    "body": "### Problem\n\nsteps to reproduce:\n\n1. open a file\n2. hit `-` to go to parent dir \n3. try to return to alt-buf via `c-^` or `:b #`\n4. nothing happens, the alt-buf was clobbered (probably by `:file` or `nvim_buf_set_name` ?)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nat minimum: don't clobber alt-buf.\n\nto fix this at the core, perhaps it would be ideal for `nvim_buf_set_name` to gain an `opts` parameter which does the dirty work of killing the old (renamed) buffer and ensuring that the original alt-buf is not changed.\n\ncc @barrettruth ",
